    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the suite is green (1 test, 0 failures). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**`memberId` composition** (e.g. `NSW2716E6609E1`):\n- **REGION** \u2014 `getRegionCode()` (`NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`, or `UNKNOWN`)\n- **FY** \u2014 2-digit fiscal-year segment of the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`\n- **HASH8** \u2014 first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over (normalized telephone + lastName), the same value used by the region-and-hash identity\n- **CHK** \u2014 single Luhn check digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 renamed the persisted field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id`; removed `getMembershipNumber()` and `getCheckDigit()`; kept `luhnCheckDigit()` (now used for the CHK segment); reworked `getFiscalYear()` to read the FY segment out of `memberId` (so it references the unified id, robust to the dedup suffix and region length).\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 replaced `customerCodeFor`/`deduplicateCustomerCode` with `memberIdFor`/`deduplicateMemberId` (collision handling now applies to `memberId`); the free-form and structured audit records now carry `memberId` (JSON key renamed to `memberId`); `primaryIdentifier` returns `getMemberId()`.\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 `localityRegion` now derives the region (used by `locality`, `timezone`, `ownerSegment`) from the `memberId` prefix.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`; added `memberId`.\n- `db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 renamed the column to `member_id` and widened it to hold the longer id (plus any dedup suffix).\n\nOne design note worth surfacing: the spec's \"the fiscal-year value \u2026 must reference the memberId\" is a little ambiguous. I read it as making `memberId` the single source of truth, so `getFiscalYear()` now extracts its FY segment from `memberId` (identical output to the old registration-date computation for created owners; `null` for seed owners that have no `memberId`, matching the prior behavior when they had no registration date). If you intended `getFiscalYear()` to keep computing directly from `registrationDate`, that's a one-line swap.",
